  "semantics": [
    "Wrapper0x36dcc fixes operand count2 then tail-calls helper0x3f6b4. Operation is unused. Helper caches output batches, first input columns and output data in native order, including required descriptor reads for zero/negative counts.",
    "Outer traversal is signed output-batch count; inner traversal is signed operand count. Each inner iteration reloads the current input descriptor pointer, row count and data pointer. Word span is cached first columns*live rows; source offset is batch*word span, all uint32 wrapped. Actual source memmove/memcpy execute for copying, including zero-length spans.",
    "Destination advances continuously by wrapped word span*4. Input descriptor/list mutation caused by earlier copies is live. First input columns and output batches remain cached even when their memory is overwritten. Opaque word payloads are copied without arithmetic.",
    "An initial native operand-count spin loop has no output/data effect and is not retained in optimized C. Its timing and interrupt/interleaving effects are outside proof; cycle identity is not claimed.",
    "REA raw bytes and callback literal0x74bdc agree with locked image: Thumb0x36dcd wrapper, shared body0x3f6b4..0x3f73f. Current Ghidra lacks function-manager entries; no fresh pseudocode is claimed.",
    "Actual C getter returns the real C wrapper relocation and probe invokes it indirectly. Source executable maps no stock code and uses no memory-function models. No public RAM normalization is applied."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Valid aligned descriptors and mapped effective memory spans are required. Zero/negative operand counts still require valid first/output descriptors due to native cache reads. Tests exercise operand counts0..3 and negative cases; large invalid lists are not assigned fallback behavior.",
    "Wrapped dimensions are tested only when their effective byte spans remain mapped. This does not establish physically valid enormous tensors.",
    "Public RAM/full FPSCR, saved R4-R11/S16-S31, SP, masks and R0 are checked.8192 private stack bytes below incoming SP and caller-clobbered scratch/APSR are outside proof. Native scratch R3 is not a promised C ABI return.",
    "All146 body bytes and58 instruction starts execute, not all inputs/interleavings. Cold FPU, timing, interrupt delivery and concurrent mutation are untested. The removed unused spin loop changes instruction timing.",
    "Probe dependency archives emit enum-size linker warnings retained in logs; called interfaces use pointer/size_t/integer types, not enums.",
    "Five callback bindings and five parent SpO2 stages remain unresolved.927-unit relocatable composition has72 application and22 boot imports. Final startup, physical sensors and complete boot remain unverified."
  ],
